  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "arrest, apprehension, capture",
      "explanation": "The act of taking someone into custody by legal authority, typically by police."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "03397_taiho_ex1",
      "japanese": "{容疑者|ようぎしゃ}が{逮捕|たいほ}された。",
      "english": "The suspect was arrested.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03397_taiho_ex2",
      "japanese": "{警察|けいさつ}は{犯人|はんにん}を{逮捕|たいほ}した。",
      "english": "The police arrested the criminal.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03397_taiho_ex3",
      "japanese": "{現行犯逮捕|げんこうはんたいほ}で{捕|つか}まった。",
      "english": "He was caught red-handed.",
      "notes": "現行犯逮捕 = arrest in the act",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {逮捕|たいほ}する (to arrest)\n- {逮捕|たいほ}される (to be arrested)\n- {逮捕状|たいほじょう} (arrest warrant)\n- {緊急逮捕|きんきゅうたいほ} (emergency arrest)\n- {現行犯逮捕|げんこうはんたいほ} (arrest on the spot, catching red-handed)\n\nRELATED LEGAL TERMS:\n- {拘束|こうそく} (detention)\n- {釈放|しゃくほう} (release)\n- {起訴|きそ} (indictment)\n- {容疑者|ようぎしゃ} (suspect)\n\nUSAGE: {逮捕|たいほ} specifically refers to arrest by authorities with legal power. For capturing in general, {捕|つか}まえる is used.",
  "cross_references": [
    {
